    "result_text": "The full test suite passes: **30 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the daily owner-creation limit (100 owners/day by `registrationDate` \u2192 429) following the codebase's established rejection-rule pattern:\n\n1. **New exception** \u2014 `rest/advice/DailyOwnerLimitExceededException.java`, mirroring the existing `CityAtCapacityException`.\n\n2. **Controller check** \u2014 In `OwnerRestControllerV1`, added a `DAILY_OWNER_LIMIT = 100` constant and a `rejectDailyOwnerLimit()` guard that counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals `LocalDate.now()` and throws when the count is \u2265 100. It's wired into `addOwner()` alongside the other reject-rules (after the city-capacity check), so it runs before the new owner is saved and reflects the pre-create state.\n\n3. **Exception handler** \u2014 Added `handleDailyOwnerLimitExceededException` to `ExceptionControllerAdvice`, translating the exception to `HttpStatus.TOO_MANY_REQUESTS` (429) via the same `ProblemDetail` builder the other handlers use.\n\nThe pre-existing `Cp19Tests` acceptance test (create 100 owners dated today, expect the 101st to be rejected with 429) now passes, and no other tests regressed.",
